# Code owners for usabl's trust-critical surface.
#
# Individual GitHub logins only. The usabl-dev org has no teams, so an
# "@usabl-dev/<name>" team reference silently resolves to nobody and routes no
# review. Each owner must also have write access to this repo, or GitHub ignores
# the entry.

# The trust boundary detects guarded-manifest divergence and drives the
# trusted-ref overlay that stops a pull request from steering scans.
/src/trust/          @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty

# The gate is the only verdict authority. Nothing else decides pass or fail.
/src/gate/           @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty

# The sequencer wires guard, coverage, scan, and gate together and applies the
# untrusted-manifest overlay. A change here can weaken the trust boundary.
/src/run.ts          @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty

# Engine configuration and the CI workflows that run the gate. A workflow edit
# could disable enforcement, so an owner reviews these too.
/usabl.config.json   @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty
/.github/workflows/  @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty

# The gate protects itself: changing who can approve policy needs owner review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty

# Every guarded path needs an owner or `usabl enforce policy` cannot be satisfied for it.
# The four below are guarded (the first two by guardedPaths in usabl.config.json, the last
# two by ALWAYS_GUARDED) and were named by no rule here, so any change to them refused
# forever with no reviewer able to clear it. The evidence floor and the waiver ledger decide
# which barriers are already accepted, and the docs and routes manifests decide what gets
# scanned at all, so a quiet edit to any of them weakens a verdict without changing a rule.
/.usabl-evidence.json @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty
/.usabl-waivers.json  @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty
/usabl.docs.json      @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty
/usabl.routes.json    @eparenti @nitin-dhevar @vishsanghishetty
